  "solution": {
    "text": "Here the given equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>RT</mi></math>.<br />On comparing with van der Waals' equation<br /><math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math><br />That is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.<br />It means only repulsive forces are present which are contributive only at very close distance so the potential energy will increase abruptly. i.e., graph C is correct.",
